ich  I'm not sure what to make out of but the  station is very much a temple inspired  building and I think I'll also sort of  theme the area around the station to be  sort of this temple or Palace ish area  and make the rest of the Japanese area  more like a smaller japanese town so  less with the quite large architecture  the station is quite large which is it's  not much larger than the Alpine station  but it's one of my worries about the  station is that it may be a bit too big  for its environment but yeah that's more  or less the fancy parts of the Japanese  area you could almost say and the rest  of the area is going to have some more  flat rights and smaller townhouses and  restaurants or at least that's the  general idea  I don't actually have an actual layouts  for it yet or any specific plans but  that'll just sort of come up in the  future and I'm not really too worried  about that and actually really looking  back at this my station was my biggest  real worry about this part of the park  since it was really the only section  where I didn't have lot of confidence in  since I already practiced quite a bit  with the Japanese theme and try to throw  out a couple of buildings and smaller  details just to see how it would  actually work out and while it's right  some smaller houses I didn't actually  try a building as large as this station  yet so that's why I was really not too  sure about it and then here at the  bottom I wanted to do this thing which  you commonly see around temples as well  they are placed on this small stone base  which is slightly raised off the ground  and they have these steps in front of  them but well that's a pretty realistic  thing I do have to say this base is way  higher than it is for any realistic  Japanese camp  which is purely because it's obviously  the station of the roller coaster and  the track is pretty high so I didn't  want to race that a bit but at least I  wanted to give it that same stone  foundation that Japanese 