le stone lanterns you might know  what I'm talking about and I think they  call them Toro which are I think are  really beautiful and I really wanted to  get along the sides here sort of along  the entranceway to the temple as you  would very often see and they don't  actually work I tried putting some  lanterns inside them but the lighting  does some strange stuff when it's inside  a chimney though that sir chimneys are  absolutely everything actually lanterns  right now as well  but yeah it means I can't exactly put  the lanterns inside the chimney which  was kind of a bummer since the lighting  just doesn't work that well so decided  in the end to put some lighting on top  of them but still the over idea is that  oh and also these plants I was so happy  with how these turned out I made a  couple of this before this a couple of  these before this video is well it's  basically a couple of wooden posts and  then just some bushes on top of it to  make some of those Japanese plants  because one of the big things at the  moment of course is the lack of  vegetation so I was really afraid that  if I would just use the legacy stuff in  there then  well it's any Park is going to end up  looking very similar to other parks  since everybody uses the same vegetation  and this is especially true for Japanese  gardens because they are very different  from European gardens and it especially  comes down to the way like they have  these trim bushes and trimmed topiary  like plants but unlike the European  topiary is where they shape them into  elephants and cones and whatnots they  have this more like flowy idea of little  so hard to describe little blobs of of  trim bushes that sort of flow in an area  and sort of like wave-like patterns and  that's something which is sort of wanted  to try my hand at quickly with those  bushes then I was actually quite happy  with how it turned out the posts don't  even look too fake and then over here I  just as a quick little entrance I wanted